    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T15:00:43Z",
    "body": "Result from the machine owner (via the user), 2026-11-19: all 3 kit programs (01 two tools, 02 peck drill, 03 rigid tap) **ran in the Robodrill's Manual Guide i graphic simulation with no alarm**. The screenshot shows O2001 (01-two-tools) loaded, `T12 M6` / `G43 H12` accepted, and the face pattern plus the contour drawn in SIMULATE-TOOLPATH.\n\nStill open (the owner will answer them later): G73 vs G83 and the R plane, M29 before G84, and where to place G05.1 Q1 R1.\n\nNotes:\n- He does not know how to change the cylinder (blank) stock shape in the Manual Guide i simulation; the kit does not need a stock shape.\n- The simulator froze once from fast button presses and the machine was powered off to recover. The programs had already run cleanly, so we do not see a G-code cause.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
